export anchor NeonAlleyStyle:
    number: 421
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Neon alley
    idea: The itinerary as a rainy side street of hanging neon signs, each leg a sign with a vertical date blade, booked legs lit in a glowing tube colour and unbooked legs dark with dashed unlit tubes, over a faint brick wall and slanted rain.
    base: dark
    palette:
        wall: #0d0b12, the page, the alley wall and the style sheet
        brick: #16121c, lower panels and swatch cards
        signBox: #0a080e, sign faces, blades, fields and list rows
        line: #2a2433, panel edges and row rules
        ink: #f4f1ff, text
        muted: #b4abc8, captions, dates and labels
        pink: #ff5fb0, the Tokyo sign, the route tube, the title glow and the primary button
        cyan: #52f3ff, the flight sign, route nodes and the secondary button
        green: #7dff9a, the Kyoto sign, Booked and Done
        violet: #c4a2ff, the flight home sign
        yellow: #ffe45c, budget digits and focus
        unlit: #6e6680, dashed unlit tubes on unbooked signs
    type:
        Body in Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow, Roboto Condensed at
        16px. Signs and the title in Arial Rounded MT Bold, Trebuchet MS,
        bold. The title 96px with a coloured neon text glow, sign titles
        26px, budget digits 40px monospace bold in yellow, blades 15px bold
        caps set vertically, labels 14px bold caps tracked 0.24em.
    layout:
        A dark wall with a faint brick grid and thin slanted rain lines over
        everything. A top row has Brightwork glowing pink and Trips plain,
        with the dates and the party on the right. The hero title reads
        Japan in cyan neon and in April in pink neon, with one muted line
        explaining that lit signs are booked. Itinerary follows as six signs
        in three columns, the middle column dropped 28px so signs hang at
        different heights. Each sign is a narrow blade with the date set
        vertically joined to a face with the date, an icon and title, the
        detail and a status pill. Lit signs use their tube colour for a 2px
        border and an outer and inner glow, the flight out cyan, Tokyo pink,
        Kyoto green and the flight home violet. The train and Osaka are
        unlit, a dashed grey tube and no glow, with Not booked unlit in a
        dashed pill. A pink pill and a cyan outlined pill follow. A row of
        four brick panels closes the screen. Route is a small neon sign with
        a pink tube joining cyan ringed Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Checklist
        lists the checks with green glowing Done or plain To do. Budget
        shows 3,200 of 5,000 euro in yellow digits over a glowing bar.
        Weather shows a cyan glowing 17 degrees and a pink blossom line.
        Below 1000px signs go two across and panels two by two, and at phone
        width all go single.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 22px between signs, alternate signs dropped 28px and 18px between lower panels.
    density: Medium. Six signs in three columns, then four small panels.
    corners: 14px sign faces joined to 12px blades, and pill status tags and buttons.
    borders: 2px tube borders in each sign colour, dashed for unlit signs, and 1px dark edges on panels.
    shadows: Neon glow in the tube colour outside and inside lit signs and round primary controls. No drop shadows.
    icons:
        2px line icons tinted in the tube colour. Booked is a check circle
        in a solid pill, Not booked a dashed circle in a dashed pill and
        Flight a plane. Done is a check and To do an open circle.
    focus: A 3px yellow outline offset 3px with a yellow glow.
    tone: Streetwise and short, such as Lit signs are booked, dark ones still need you.
